# Caddy in front of the portal. SITE_ADDRESS comes from .env.
#
# `tls internal`: Caddy signs the certificate with its own local CA. Browsers
# warn once ("not private"), which is the price of having no company domain
# yet. With a real domain that resolves publicly, delete the `tls internal`
# line and Caddy fetches a Let's Encrypt certificate on its own; with a
# company certificate, use `tls /path/cert.pem /path/key.pem` instead.
#
# No `log` directive on purpose: Caddy writes no access log unless asked,
# and an access log would undo the anonymity rules (docs/anonymity.md).

{$SITE_ADDRESS} {
	tls internal
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy portal:3000
}
